From 97397e48c9edce5786da54d65b50184c0cae65c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wmehanna <wassimmehanna@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:43:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] perf(tcg): let DSB skip vCPUs that cannot see the flushed
 entries

A DSB after a broadcast TLBI waited for every running vCPU. A vCPU
between TBs (P80_BC=quiet) or running in another ASID (P85_BC=asid)
cannot touch the entries and is skipped. Both are on by default,
P80_BC=off and P85_BC=off turn them off. Includes the P80/P85 guest
sampler and statistics, off unless P80_DIR is set, and a
broken-on-purpose negative control (P80_BC=nowait) for the TLB tests.
---
 accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c       |  25 ++-
 accel/tcg/cputlb.c         |  94 +++++++++++-
 accel/tcg/meson.build      |   1 +
 accel/tcg/p80.c            | 306 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 accel/tcg/translate-all.c  |   5 +
 include/hw/core/cpu.h      |  18 +++
 include/qemu/p80.h         |  74 +++++++++
 system/cpus.c              |  15 +-
 target/arm/cpu.c           |  37 +++++
 target/arm/tcg/tlb-insns.c |  28 +++-
 10 files changed, 588 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 accel/tcg/p80.c
 create mode 100644 include/qemu/p80.h

